After several weeks of hiatus, I finally took care of the ascension
run for Melody the Priest, whose previous dead incarnations had been
littering the Hearse archives for weeks before.

She started with spellbooks of healing and identify, which are
probably the best possible two for a priest.  She found a hardware
store stocked with _four_ magic lamps, and with a certain amount of
stubbornness attempted to go as wishless as possible.  I actually
can't remember what the wishes were, but at the end, she'd used only
two wishes.  I'm reasonably certain she didn't have to wish for GDSM
because she found it in a bones pile, but I could be wrong.

In any case, the ascension was genoless, polyless, and polyselfless.
The ascension run was mostly unexciting, except for getting absolutely
swamped by critters in the area of Moloch's sanctum.  If it hadn't
been for a very convenient rubber chicken, I might still be fighting
my way out of there.

That takes care of Priest and Valkyrie in this version of Nethack.  I
think I'll do Monks next for a while, and if I get burned out on that,
do a wombat type.


